## Project Overview
This is a Jekyll-based personal portfolio website for Chinmay Singh. Follow these rules to maintain code quality, consistency, and best practices while reflecting his authentic voice and goals.

## File Structure & Organization

### Core Jekyll Files
- `_config.yml` - Site configuration (update title, description, social links)
- `Gemfile` - Ruby dependencies
- `index.markdown` - Homepage
- `about.markdown` - About page
- `404.html` - Custom 404 page
- `_posts/` - Blog posts directory

### Content Organization
- Keep blog posts in `_posts/` with YYYY-MM-DD-title.md format
- Use descriptive, SEO-friendly filenames
- Organize assets in logical folders (images, css, js)

## Jekyll Best Practices

### Front Matter
- Always include front matter in markdown files
- Use consistent front matter structure:
```yaml
---
layout: post
title: "Your Title"
date: YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS
categories: [category1, category2]
tags: [tag1, tag2]
author: Your Name
---
```

### Liquid Templates
- Always use correct Liquid syntax: `{{ variable }}` for outputting values, and `{% tag %}` for logic or control flow.
- Escape HTML output when necessary to prevent rendering iss
### Liquid Templates
- Use proper Liquid syntax: `{{ variable }}` for output, `{% tag %}` for logic
- Escape HTML when needed: `{{ content | escape }}`
- Use `{% raw %}` and `{% endraw %}` for code examples
ues or XSS vulnerabilities, e.g., `{{ content | escape }}`.
- For displaying raw Liquid code in documentation or blog posts, wrap code blocks with `{% raw %}` and `{% endraw %}`.
- Comment complex Liquid logic for clarity and future maintenance.
- Use whitespace control (`{{-` and `-}}`, `{%-` and `-%}`) to manage output formatting when needed.

### Configuration
- Update `_config.yml` with your personal information
- Set proper `url` and `baseurl` for production
- Configure social media usernames
- Add SEO meta tags

## Content Guidelines

### Blog Posts
- Write in clear, professional language
- Use proper markdown formatting
- Include relevant images with alt text
- Add meta descriptions for SEO
- Use categories and tags consistently

### Portfolio Content
- Showcase your best work first
- Include project descriptions, technologies used, and links
- Add case studies for major projects
- Keep content updated and relevant

## Code Quality Standards

### Markdown
- Use proper heading hierarchy (H1 → H2 → H3)
- Include alt text for all images
- Use code blocks with language specification
- Keep line length under 80 characters where possible

### HTML/CSS
- Use semantic HTML elements
- Ensure responsive design
- Optimize images for web
- Follow accessibility guidelines (WCAG 2.1)

### JavaScript
- Write clean, well-documented code
- Use modern ES6+ syntax
- Minimize external dependencies
- Ensure cross-browser compatibility

## SEO & Performance

### SEO Best Practices
- Include meta descriptions on all pages
- Use proper heading structure
- Optimize images with descriptive filenames
- Add structured data where appropriate
- Create an XML sitemap

### Performance Optimization
- Compress images before uploading
- Minimize CSS and JavaScript
- Use lazy loading for images
- Optimize for Core Web Vitals

## Development Workflow

### Local Development
- Use `bundle exec jekyll serve` for local development
- Test changes in multiple browsers
- Validate HTML and CSS
- Check for broken links

### Version Control
- Commit frequently with descriptive messages
- Use feature branches for major changes
- Keep sensitive information out of commits
- Document configuration changes

## Security Considerations

### Data Protection
- Never commit API keys or passwords
- Use environment variables for sensitive data
- Sanitize user inputs if any
- Keep dependencies updated

### Content Security
- Validate all external links
- Use HTTPS for all external resources
- Implement proper CSP headers if needed

## Accessibility Standards

### WCAG Compliance
- Ensure proper color contrast ratios
- Use semantic HTML elements
- Provide alt text for images
- Ensure keyboard navigation works
- Test with screen readers

### Inclusive Design
- Write content for diverse audiences
- Use clear, simple language
- Provide multiple ways to access content
- Consider mobile users

## Testing & Quality Assurance

### Content Review
- Proofread all content before publishing
- Check grammar and spelling
- Verify all links work
- Test on different devices

### Technical Testing
- Validate HTML and CSS
- Test responsive design
- Check loading speed
- Verify SEO elements

## Deployment Guidelines

### GitHub Pages
- Use `github-pages` gem for deployment
- Configure custom domain properly
- Set up proper redirects
- Monitor for build errors

### Performance Monitoring
- Use Google PageSpeed Insights
- Monitor Core Web Vitals
- Track user analytics
- Monitor for broken links

## Maintenance

### Regular Updates
- Keep Jekyll and plugins updated
- Review and update content regularly
- Monitor for security vulnerabilities
- Backup content regularly

### Content Strategy
- Plan content calendar
- Update portfolio projects
- Keep blog posts current
- Engage with audience

## Code Style Guidelines

### YAML
- Use consistent indentation (2 spaces)
- Quote strings when needed
- Use arrays for multiple values
- Keep configuration organized

### Markdown
- Use consistent formatting
- Include proper spacing
- Use tables for structured data
- Keep code blocks clean

### CSS/SCSS
- Use consistent naming conventions
- Organize styles logically
- Comment complex rules
- Use CSS custom properties for theming

## Documentation

### Code Comments
- Comment complex Liquid logic
- Document custom functions
- Explain configuration choices
- Keep README updated

### Content Documentation
- Document content guidelines
- Maintain style guide
- Keep asset inventory
- Document deployment process

## Emergency Procedures

### Backup Strategy
- Regular backups of content
- Version control for all changes
- Document recovery procedures
- Test backup restoration

### Troubleshooting
- Common Jekyll issues and solutions
- Debugging build errors
- Performance optimization steps
